een denylist and mkdir). Four nits carry forward.\\\",\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SAFE-MAJ-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"parse_entry_repo greedy regex extracts the LAST em-dash-separated repo segment from a single +### diff line. A malformed log header '### TIMESTAMP — jrnb2024/decoy@main — jrnb2024/target@main' (one line → one +### match → satisfies exactly-one assertion) yields group(1)='jrnb2024/target' via greedy .+ backtracking to the final — segment. If DISPATCH-NOTE declares **Target:** jrnb2024/target, the target-match passes even when the actual enable-required-check.sh invocation ran against jrnb2024/decoy.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"check-invocation-log-entry.sh lines 254–266: parse_entry_repo regex r'^###\\\\\\\\s+.+\\\\\\\\s+—\\\\\\\\s+([A-Za-z0-9._-]+(?:/[A-Za-z0-9._-]+)?)@([A-Za-z0-9._/-]+)$' — .+ is greedy with no possessive or atomic qualifier; re.search backtracks to match the rightmost \\\\\\\\s+—\\\\\\\\s+ separator. No test exercises a single +### line containing two repo segments. The exactly-one-LINE assertion (len(matched) != 1) is correct but insufficient: it prevents two separate log entries, not two repos on one header line.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"An operator (or careless copy-paste from documentation showing multiple repos) can craft a single log header that passes all enforced checks while the first (visible) repo differs from what was actually onboarded. Audit-trail integrity of the target-match invariant 2 is undermined. Exploitability is limited to the single operator in D-031 mode but the bypass path is untested and structurally silent.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"After group(1) extraction, assert the header contains exactly one em-dash-separated segment before the @-delimited branch: verify line[1:] has at most one occurrence of ' — ' (or equivalently count re.findall of the em-dash separator pattern). Alternatively anchor the timestamp pattern: ^###\\\\\\\\s+\\\\\\\\d{4}-\\\\\\\\d{2}-\\\\\\\\d{2}T[^—]+—\\\\\\\\s+([...]+)@([...]+)$ without .+ backtracking. Add a diff-base test case with one +### line containing two — segments to cover the regression path.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"MIN-SAFE-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Slug canonicalization collision allows a false-positive STATUS.md TF-row match. Two adopter repos that differ only by . or _ (e.g. jrnb2024/repo.pim and jrnb2024/repo-pim both canonicalize to jrnb2024-repo-pim). Adopter B's already-present TF-024X-renovate-jrnb2024-repo-pim row satisfies adopter A's onboarded-operator-bump STATUS.md check.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"canonicalize_adopter_slug (lines 110–116) replaces [^a-z0-9-] with '-'. The onboarded-operator-bump STATUS.md pattern uses rf'TF-024X-renovate-{re.escape(slug)}...' (exact slug match). D-044 acknowledges 'cohort repo names must remain unique after canonicalization' but no runtime collision check exists. The current 5-cohort names do not collide; the gap is systemic for future cohort expansions.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"A future cohort adopter whose name canonicalises to an existing slug gets a false-positive CI pass on the STATUS.md check without a fresh TF row, silently satisfying the onboarded-operator-bump gate for the wrong adopter.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add a precomputed collision check script or a comment in canonicalize_adopter_slug with an explicit D-045 gating criterion requiring operator verification of slug uniqueness across all cohort adopters before 024C opens.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"MIN-SAFE-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"TOCTOU window between the readlink/realpath denylist check and mkdir -p + sed write calls in scaffold-downstream.sh. A concurrent actor with write access to OUTPUT_DIR's parent can atomically replace the directory with a symlink to a system path between the denylist check and the first mkdir call, redirecting scaffolder output to a denied location.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"scaffold-downstream.sh: OUTPUT_DIR resolved