.M ^ anchor without leading-whitespace allowance); indented occurrences are invisible to the guard by design.'\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"nit-SAFE-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"test_scaffold_downstream.sh YAML validation silently exits 0 with a SKIP message when pyyaml is absent. In minimal CI environments the only structural YAML validation of the emitted wrapper is skipped without the test failing.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Lines 133–134 of test_scaffold_downstream.sh: python3 -c 'import yaml' 2>/dev/null || { echo 'SKIP: pyyaml not installed; YAML validation skipped'; return 0; }. The yaml module (pyyaml) is not part of the Python standard library and may be absent in stripped CI images.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"A template change producing invalid YAML would not be caught in environments without pyyaml; every adopter wrapper would be silently malformed.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Verify pyyaml availability in CI pre-requisites, or add a fallback check using python3 -c 'import yaml; yaml.safe_load(...)' noting that ubuntu-24.04 GitHub Actions runners include python3-yaml by default.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"nit-SAFE-003\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"SCP_REPO_ROOT environment variable, if set by the operator to a fork containing the same template file, redirects the --scp-sha existence check and HEAD-lineage warning to the wrong repository. A SHA absent from the upstream SCP repo but present in the fork passes exit-2 validation.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"scaffold-downstream.sh line 14: SCP_REPO_ROOT=${SCP_REPO_ROOT:-$(cd ... && pwd)}; git operations at lines 149–165 all use -C $SCP_REPO_ROOT. The only identity check is template file existence (lines 53–55), present in any fork.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Operator with SCP_REPO_ROOT pointing to a fork can emit a wrapper pinned to a fork-only SHA, referencing a potentially diverged or experimental commit. Low severity in single-operator mode.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add a one-time remot