 either abort or (if the test harness is lenient) produce false negatives, giving false confidence in a broken scaffolder.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a preflight: `git -C \\\\\\\"$REPO_ROOT\\\\\\\" cat-file -e \\\\\\\"$SCP_SHA\\\\\\\" 2>/dev/null || { echo 'SKIP: v1.0.0 commit absent (shallow clone)'; exit 0; }`. Alternatively fetch the tag explicitly in CI setup.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"MAJ-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJOR\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"SAFE-003 phantom-2-entry enforcement (parse_entry_repo exactly-one assertion) is tested only in --pr mode (case17). The --diff-base code path has no equivalent test, leaving a regression gap for the local operator workflow.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh case17 uses a fake-gh stub emitting 2 +### lines for --pr mode. Grep of the test file for diff-base phantom/2-entry confirms no analogous test exists for `git diff --unified=0` producing 2 +### lines.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"A regression in the --diff-base branch_log_patch parse path (e.g., a changed unified=0 context stripping the + prefix) would not be caught by the test suite, allowing multi-entry confusion for local operator runs.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a diff-base variant: create a scratch git repo with two commits each adding a +### entry, run the script with --diff-base pointing to the first commit, and assert exit 1 with the \\\\\\\"expected exactly one\\\\\\\" error.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"MIN-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MINOR\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"V1_0_0_SCP_SHA constant in scaffold-downstream.sh is not validated against the v1.0.0 git tag at runtime; a drifted constant would silently emit wrong TF-023E-002 skip-warnings.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"scaffold-downstream.sh line 16: `V1_0_0_SCP_SHA=\\\\\\\"41a529908ef5355b82ca924ef0502fa5ec2fcc11\\\\\\\"`. The post-v1.2.0 branch (lines 154-158) uses this constant as the comparator. Test line 172 checks the string, but only at test time.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"If the constant is manually edited incorrectly during a future update, operators pinning the v1.0.0 SHA would silently receive no TF-023E-002 warning, defeating the scorecard permissions guardrail.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a one-time assertion at script startup: `expected_v1_sha=\\\\\\\"$(git -C \\\\\\\"$SCP_REPO_ROOT\\\\\\\" rev-parse v1.0.0 2>/dev/null || true)\\\\\\\"; [ -z \\\\\\\"$expected_v1_sha\\\\\\\" ] || [ \\\\\\\"$expected_v1_sha\\\\\\\" = \\\\\\\"$V1_0_0_SCP_SHA\\\\\\\" ] || warn \\\\\\\"V1_0_0_SCP_SHA constant mismatch — update the script\\\\\\\"`.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"MIN-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MINOR\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"U+2014 em dash literal in parse_entry_repo regex is not defended against encoding corruption; a substituted U+2013 en dash silently causes all onboarded/onboarded-operator-bump enforcements to fail with 'expected exactly one log entry target match, found 0'.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"check-invocation-log-entry.sh line 259: regex contains a literal — (U+2014). The comment at line 250-252 acknowledges the em dash dependency but provides no runtime defense. The branch-protection-log emitter in 024B-extras uses the same literal.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Copy-paste from a PDF or rich-text editor substituting en dash would cause every --pr and --diff-base invocation for onboarded status to exit 1 with a misleading 'found 0' message, blocking all cascade merges until the corruption is diagnosed.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Use a Unicode escape in the regex: `\\\\\\\\u2014` via Python's re engine (`\\\\\\\\N{EM DASH}` or `\\\\\\\\u2014`), or match `[ \\\\\\\\u2013\\\\\\\\u2014-]` to accept near-miss variants with a warning.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"MIN-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MINOR\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"non_head_sha selection in test_scaffold_downstream.sh relies on SCP_SHA_POST_V1_2_0 always equalling main HEAD; if these diverge the non-HEAD warn-path test exercises the wrong SHA and may not trigger the expected warning.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"test_scaffold_downstream.sh lines 227-228: `non_head_sha=\\\\\\\"$SCP_SHA_POST_V1_2_0\\\\\\\"`. SCP_SHA_POST_V1_2_0 is resolved as `git rev-parse main || git rev-parse HEAD` — identical to the main_head_sha used in the non-HEAD comparison. The test comment does not document this dependency.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Low probability of breaking now; high probability of silent test degradation after a branch restructure or if the test is ported to a detached HEAD CI context where main and HEAD differ.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Select non_head_sha as `git rev-parse HEAD^` (parent of HEAD) and add a guard that HEAD has at least one parent; this is always distinct from main HEAD and exercises the actual warn path robustly.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"nit-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"NIT\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"fail-closed die() call at check-invocation-log-entry.sh line 197 uses exit 1 (default), inconsistent with all other input-validation errors which use exit 2.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Line 197: `die \\\\\\\"FAIL-CLOSED: cascade-status field absent or unrecognised...\\\\\\\"` — no second arg, so die() uses `exit ${2:-1}`. All other die() calls with exit 2 are for bad invocation/input. Exit 1 is conventionally \\\\\\\"policy check failed\\\\\\\"; exit 2 is \\\\\\\"bad arguments\\\\\\\".\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Callers inspecting exit codes to distinguish \\\\\\\"bad invocation\\\\\\\" (exit 2) from \\\\\\\"policy check failed\\\\\\\" (exit 1) cannot tell whether an absent cascade-status is a scripting error or a genuine policy failure. Low operational impact but inconsistent contract.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Pass explicit exit code: `die \\\\\\\"FAIL-CLOSED: cascade-status field absent or unrecognised; must be one of {...}\\\\\\\" 2` — treating absent/unrecognised status as a bad-input error consistent with all other validation failures.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"nit-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"NIT\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"D-044 decision body is a dense single-paragraph block (~1200 chars) that is hard to scan; no structural issue, but readability is lower than if it used a brief rationale + bullet impact list.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"docs/DECISIONS.md D-044 row: single paragraph covering split rationale, scope, deferral, SCOPE-CORRECTION reference, and FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 all concatenated. Peers D-041/D-042/D-043 follow the same format.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"No correctness impact. Future operators triaging a cascade failure may take longer to parse the decision context.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"No fix required for correctness. Optional: split into a 1-sentence rationale followed by 3-4 bullet points in a future documentation pass.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"566dfcb7-33f5-460d-bece-0d8c28ba0f6d\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.807002,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1512,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":82597,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":230263,\"output_tokens\":60250,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":82597,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":3,\"output_tokens\":3112,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":7381,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":17551,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":17551},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":2397,\"outputTokens\":27,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.002532,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":2911,\"outputTokens\":68053,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":341815,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":179306,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.80447,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"2d735dcb-c14a-4955-8f87-bcd77af966c6\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
