{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/r1-completeness_governance.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":484524,\"duration_api_ms\":485211,\"num_turns\":16,\"result\":\"Now I have everything needed. Let me produce the review JSON.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"reviewer_lens\\\":\\\"completeness_governance\\\",\\\"slice_id\\\":\\\"WP-SCP-024/024B-core\\\",\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"APPROVED_WITH_NOTES\\\",\\\"crit_count\\\":0,\\\"maj_count\\\":0,\\\"min_count\\\":3,\\\"nit_count\\\":2,\\\"summary\\\":\\\"024B-core scope is internally coherent and complete. All five cascade-status check-paths (4 enforcement + not-applicable carve-out) are implemented in check-invocation-log-entry.sh and tested exhaustively. Plan-doc invariant 2 regex is implemented byte-for-byte. Scaffolder emits 4 files with correct substitutions, system-path denylist, bootstrap guard, and MANIFEST SHA256 audit. Template carries Renovate marker and least-privilege permissions. Extras carve-outs are confirmed clean (no --restore content, no .github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml, no §12.8 break-glass). SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md supplies empirical R6→R7→R8 trajectory justification and explicit anti-descope framing. D-044 is correctly scoped to core deliverables with SCOPE-CORRECTION cited. STATUS.md chain entry documents split decision, branch references, and plan-doc §6 amendment. Both FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 and TF-024B-SCAFFOLDER-023E002-UPDATE are filed and named. VERSIONING.md alignment holds: scaffolder, template, and CI script are all internal-only surfaces requiring no version bump. Three MIN issues and two nits found; none block merge.\\\",\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-MIN-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Duplicate temp-directory name case15c in test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh: two distinct test scenarios both initialize $TMPDIR/case15c.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh: repo_dir=$TMPDIR/case15c used at line ~433 (phantom-2-entry duplicate cascade-status test) and again at line ~625 (not-applicable without --tooling-slice-id). init_case_repo reinitializes the directory on the second call, overwriting git history from the first case.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"If the first case15c test fails and the test suite exits early, the second case15c is silently skipped. If run in a modified order, git history carryover from the first initialization could mask regressions in the second scenario. Fragile rather than immediately broken.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Rename the phantom-2-entry case to case15c-phantom (or case15c-dup) and renumber accordingly. Trivial find-and-replace.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-MIN-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Plan-doc §5.3 states MANIFEST.json lists 'every file emitted + its SHA256 for audit'; D-044 echoes the same wording. Neither documents that MANIFEST.json self-excludes from its own sha256 entries.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh emits 3 entries in manifest.files (wrapper, CODEOWNERS-snippet, CASCADE-PR-BODY). test_scaffold_downstream.sh line ~76 asserts len(payload['files']) != 3 with comment 'MANIFEST.json intentionally excludes itself from its own sha256 entries to avoid circular dependency'. Plan-doc §5.3 and D-044 do not mention self-exclusion.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Future maintainer reading plan-doc or D-044 expects MANIFEST to include itself in sha256 tracking. Minor audit-trail ambiguity: a forensic analyst counting entries sees 3 not 4 without explanation in the governing documents.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add a parenthetical to plan-doc §5.3 and D-044: '(MANIFEST.json itself excluded from its own sha256 entries to avoid circular dependency)'.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-MIN-003\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Plan-doc §6 024C row AC column omits 024B-extras-merged and FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001-closed as inline prerequisites, forcing operators to cross-reference two other locations.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Plan-doc §6 024C AC: 'PIM policy-check / scp/policy-check required-check live; ≥1 Renovate-bump-propagation cycle merged clean; D-045 filed.' The 024B-extras gate is only in the 024B row ('024B-extras must also merge before 024C opens') and the post-table '024B split note'. The FUP gate appears in STATUS.md tracked-forward items. No inline mention in the 024C row itself.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"At 024C authoring time the operator must consult the 024B row, post-table note, and STATUS.md to reconstruct the full predecessor set. Scatter increases risk of premature 024C open if a future operator skips the cross-references.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Prepend to 024C AC column: 'Hard prerequisites: 024B-core merged + 024B-extras merged + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closed. Then:' followed by existing criteria.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-nit-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"DISPATCH-NOTE footer status reads 'DRAFT v0.1 — awaiting Codex T3 surgical-clean dispatch' despite the slice being well past dispatch into fix-round 8 and R1 review.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/DISPATCH-NOTE.md line 99: '**Status:** DRAFT v0.1 — awaiting Codex T3 surgical-clean dispatch.' Git log shows fix-round-7 and fix-round-8 commits; r1-*.json files are being written.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Stale label causes reviewer confusion about the slice's actual lifecycle phase.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Update to '**Status:** R1 review in progress (fix-round 8 closed; awaiting fixpoint).'\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-nit-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Fail-closed error message in check-invocation-log-entry.sh lists 'not applicable' in the recognized set without clarifying the --allow-not-applicable flag requirement.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"check-invocation-log-entry.sh line ~197: 'FAIL-CLOSED: cascade-status field absent or unrecognised; must be one of {onboarded, onboarded-operator-bump, blocked-on-adopter-conflict, not applicable}'. Plan-doc §2 invariant 2's fail-closed enumeration is {onboarded, onboarded-operator-bump, blocked-on-adopter-conflict} (3 values). 'not applicable' requires --allow-not-applicable flag.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"A 024C-F cohort slice operator who accidentally uses 'cascade-status: not applicable' will first receive the fail-closed message listing 'not applicable' as valid, then a second separate error requiring --allow-not-applicable. Minor UX confusion; not a safety bypass.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Amend error message: 'must be one of {onboarded, onboarded-operator-bump, blocked-on-adopter-conflict} for cohort slices; not applicable is for tooling slices only and requires --allow-not-applicable).'\\\"}]}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"7a0b8d7e-aa0e-4c0e-b4d4-714d4dfb354a\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.0218338999999999,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":11,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":129446,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":612898,\"output_tokens\":23397,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":129446,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":1893,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":136532,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":295,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":295},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1434,\"outputTokens\":24,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.001554,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":11,\"outputTokens\":23397,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":612898,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":129446,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.0202798999999998,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"72592582-99d5-4d7c-9b9c-ea401ebe9806\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
